WEBVTT

00:45:28.458 --> 00:45:31.268
is that it empowers the people
you know to ask.

00:45:31.292 --> 00:45:32.559
EP: I would hope that.

00:45:32.583 --> 00:45:35.768
AG: Because I know that you
will never be offended by a request

00:45:35.792 --> 00:45:38.018
because you think
that part of a relationship

00:45:38.042 --> 00:45:41.101
is people should be able to ask
anything they want of each other

00:45:41.125 --> 00:45:43.393
and they should also have
the freedom to refuse

00:45:43.417 --> 00:45:45.851
if they think it's not
appropriate or not possible.

00:45:45.875 --> 00:45:49.393
Which is very helpful for those of us
who struggle to ask for help.

00:45:49.417 --> 00:45:51.143
EP: That is true, that is true.

00:45:51.167 --> 00:45:52.476
I think, you know,

00:45:52.500 --> 00:45:55.518
there's a question
I love to ask in the workspace

00:45:55.542 --> 00:45:57.684
that I used to ask in a very different way

00:45:57.708 --> 00:45:59.601
when I used to do cross-cultural work,

00:45:59.625 --> 00:46:01.684
but it has become
suddenly really relevant.